@nsobid-867B345248124EF3D70E3202E221E978964C592F

# Xenoblade Chronicles 2 3.0.1 - Fix Loading Hang

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Fixes a stock hang where a loading screen never finishes, most often right
// after skipping a cutscene, and more often the higher the frame rate. This
// patches the nnSdk module, not the game's main module, so it applies with or
// without the frame rate mods.
//
// The game reads its archives through four file threads that share a pool of
// two IPC sessions to the filesystem service. A thread that finds the pool
// empty sleeps on a condition variable until a session is returned. Returning
// a session wakes one sleeper, but only when the pool was empty at that
// moment. With two threads asleep, two sessions returned back to back wake
// only one of them: the second return sees the first session still in the
// pool and wakes nobody. The other thread sleeps on with a free session in the
// pool, and the load waits on its read forever, since no other thread issues
// filesystem calls to wake it. Loading bursts after a cutscene skip put
// several threads in the queue at once, and a higher frame rate issues
// streaming reads more often, so the window opens more often.
//
// Every returned session now wakes one sleeper. A woken thread rechecks the
// pool under the lock and goes back to sleep if another thread took the
// session first, so the extra wakeups are harmless.
@enabled
// HipcSimpleClientSessionManagerBase::Impl::Deallocate: always signal
000525EC 1F2003D5   // NOP = wake a waiter on every return (was CBNZ X8, skip the signal when the pool was not empty)
// HipcSimpleClientSessionManagerBase::Impl::SetSessionCountImpl: same, per added session
0005267C 1F2003D5   // NOP = wake a waiter for every added session (was CBNZ X8, skip the signal when the pool was not empty)
@stop

// Byte-verified against the nnSdk image in memory.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
